<title>USA: U.S. Dec import prices rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Dec import prices rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Department report of U.S. import and export price changes by percent (unadjusted).</p>
<p>    -			    Dec    Nov-Rev from  Dec 96/95</p>
<p> ALL IMPORTS		   0.1   -0.2   -0.1	1.3</p>
<p> -Petroleum		    0.3   -0.8   -0.1     31.7</p>
<p> -Nonpetroleum		 0.1   -0.1   -0.2     -1.7</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	 -1.2    0.3   -0.6     -0.7</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies	0.3   -0.1    0.1	8.2</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	     -0.3   -0.5   -0.5     -4.0</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts     0.3   -0.2   -0.2     UNCH</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos   0.1   -0.1   UNCH     -0.6</p>
<p>Percent changes, not seasonally adjusted --</p>
<p> ALL EXPORTS		  UNCH   -0.4   -0.5     -1.2</p>
<p> -Agricultural		-0.9   -2.3   -2.8     -6.9</p>
<p> -Non-Agricultural	   0.1   UNCH   -0.1     -0.4</p>
<p> -Food, Feed, Drink	 -1.2   -1.8   -2.6     -6.5</p>
<p> -Industrial Supplies	0.4   -0.6   -0.5     -2.3</p>
<p> -Capital Goods	     -0.1   UNCH   UNCH     UNCH</p>
<p> -Motor Vehicles,Parts    UNCH    0.2    0.2	0.5</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods ExAutos   0.2   UNCH   UNCH	1.5</p>
<p>The department reported December price indexes (1990 base year equals 100) of 108.2 for imports, and 108.1 for exports.</p>
</text>
